  "conclusion": "A QuickHelp key names a control and does not locate one. The only canonical link from a key to a screen is the nib `qhid` runtime attribute, and it reaches 587 of 9835 keys -- 5.97%. The coverage is not spread thinly, it is concentrated: Preferences at 93.4% and Song Settings at 88.5%, and ZERO for the global menus, the mixer window menu, the project audio browser and the global tracks. Those are the surfaces this repository drives. Every key an Anchor could place is an Anchor into a Help Book Apple does not ship on disk, so that route is not a local canonical fact either. The practical consequence for the locale migration is a bound rather than a blocker: AXHelp names a control already in hand, which is enough to READ a surface and to refuse the wrong element, and it is not enough to FIND one. Finding still needs the structural walk this repository already does.",
  "limits": [
    "Read from the bundle only. Whether a control whose nib carries a qhid actually exposes it through the accessibility tree was not measured; the one earlier live reading found 1 of 86 matched controls carrying one.",
    "The families are grouped by the key's alphabetic prefix, which is this repository's reading of the naming scheme and not something Apple documents.",
    "The 32 qhid values naming no QuickHelp key were not explained -- dead wiring and version drift are both consistent with what was seen.",
    "The Anchor route was refuted for LOCAL data. The mapping exists over the network and two anchors were resolved there by hand; that is not a canonical source this repository can pin.",
    "Nothing here measures the numeric-triple keys, which are 4,061 of the 9,835 and have zero nib coverage by construction: plug-in editors are not built from nibs."
  ],
